{
  "title": "Malignant Peripheral Nerve Sheath Tumor",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8055/malignant-peripheral-nerve-sheath-tumor",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jul 23 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Malignant Peripheral Nerve Sheath Tumors, also known as neurofibrosarcoma or malignant schwannoma, are malignant tumors that may occur as solitary lesions or be associated with neurofibromatosis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition usually presents in patients between 20 and 50 years old with soft-tissue masses associated with a peripheral nerve or prior neurofibroma.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with a biopsy showing spindle cells with wavy nuclei resembling fibrosarcoma. Immunostaining is positive for S100.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually wide surgical resection and radiation.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "30 to 55 years for solitary neurofibromas",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "20 to 40 years for neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF-1)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most cases associated with NF-1",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "4% incidence in these patients",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Presentation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "soft-tissue mass",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most arise from large nerves (sciatic, brachial plexus)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "motor and sensory deficit of the affected nerve",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiograph",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually normal or non-specific soft-tissue mass",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "low-intensity on T1-weighted images",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "high intensity on T2-weighted images",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8055/images/malignant%20schwannoma%20mri.jpg",
                  "caption": "Axial MRI demonstrating MPNST arising from sciatic nerve"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "serial MRI may show enlargement of previous benign nerve sheath lesion suggesting malignant transformation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bone scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mildly positive",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Histology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "classic characteristics are",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**spindle cells with wavy nuclei resembling fibrosarcoma**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8055/images/malignant%20schwannoma%20path.jpg",
                      "caption": "pathology section demonstrating MPNST"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Immunohistochemistry",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**positive S100** stain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**keratin staining** is negative",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "wide surgical resection + radiation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "standard of care in most patients",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "in general, treated as high-grade sarcoma",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "wide resection should include entire affected nerve",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "radiation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "perform preoperative neo-adjuvant radiation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "chemotherapy not useful",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Survival for solitary lesion is 75% (5-year survival)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Survival associated with NF-1 is 30% (5-year survival)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
